# Palomar Comparator safety

- Read `docs/PALOMAR_STYLE.md` before changing compared declarations.
- Pin universe parameter names and make unstable instance paths explicit.
- Keep every `definition_names` value and every transitively locked
  Challenge/Solution definition structurally identical.
- Audit named child definitions referenced by matching parent bodies; Palomar
  compares those values independently.
- Never use inline proofs in locked structure values: generated
  `._proof_N` constants are mechanically compared.
- Move proof fields to named theorems and list them in `theorem_names`.
- Challenge may contain proof holes; Solution and `Scott1972/**/*.lean` may not.
- Run `scripts/palomar_preflight.sh` after relevant edits and before a
  submission commit. Do not claim readiness unless it passes.
